# Citation metadata for compresso-recsys.
# After the first Zenodo archive of a release, add the concept DOI as `doi:`
# (it always resolves to the latest version). A paper describing compresso-recsys
# is under submission; when it is published, add it as `preferred-citation`.
# Validate with:  pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use compresso-recsys in your research, please cite this software
  release using the metadata below.
title: "compresso-recsys"
abstract: >-
  A toolkit for practical recommender development in three parts usable alone
  or together: one data checkpoint (interaction matrix, sequences, item
  metadata, embeddings and splits in one portable file with recorded
  provenance), a model base class for collaborative, sequential, cold-start and
  multimodal recommenders, and evaluation with paired statistical testing.
type: software
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/zombak79/compresso-recsys"
url: "https://zombak79.github.io/compresso-recsys/"
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - evaluation
  - statistical significance testing
  - reproducibility
  - datasets
  - cold-start
  - sequential recommendation
